# The `pocketcasts` tool: the std/go worker image (named by locator, at the
# same caos revision as flake.lock) with worker.go curried onto it, plus the
# `help` it is described by. `@call` makes each call its own run: without it an
# identical call would be answered from the result cache, and a library that
# changed since would read as stale.
HELP=<<END
Read and change a Pocket Casts account: subscriptions, folders, and which
episodes of a podcast are archived. Pocket Casts has no public API; this uses the
endpoints the official open-source Android app uses, with the account email and
password from the pocketcasts-email and pocketcasts-password secrets.

The result is plain text, tab-separated where it is a table. A failure is a
failed run with the reason. A write is read back afterwards and reported as
confirmed or NOT CONFIRMED. Destructive operations (unsubscribe, delete_folder,
archive, unarchive) only describe what they would do until apply=true: show the
user that description and get their go-ahead before repeating the call with it.

@param op One of: list_podcasts, list_folders, search, subscribe, unsubscribe, move_podcast, create_folder, rename_folder, delete_folder, list_episodes, archive, unarchive, selftest (offline check of the protobuf encoder).
@param [podcast] A podcast: its uuid, or part of its title (must match exactly one subscribed podcast, or exactly one by full title). unsubscribe and move_podcast take several, comma-separated. subscribe takes uuids only.
@param [folder] A folder: its uuid or name, or none for no folder. list_podcasts: only that folder's podcasts. move_podcast: the destination. subscribe: put the new podcast there. rename_folder, delete_folder: the folder.
@param [name] create_folder: the new folder's name. rename_folder: its new name.
@param [color] create_folder: an integer color index (default 0).
@param [query] search: text to search the Pocket Casts directory for (best effort; the endpoint is unverified).
@param [with-latest] list_podcasts: true to also fetch each podcast's latest episode date and episode count (one request per podcast; use it to find dormant podcasts).
@param [from-number] list_episodes, archive, unarchive: lowest episode number to include. Numbers come from the feed if it has them, else are parsed from the title ("#102", "Episode 102", a leading number); see number-regex. Episodes with no number never match a number filter.
@param [to-number] Highest episode number to include (inclusive).
@param [number-regex] Regex with one capture group that extracts the episode number from the title, overriding the default parsing.
@param [title-regex] Only episodes whose title matches this regex (Go syntax, add (?i) for case-insensitive).
@param [published_after] Only episodes published on or after this date, YYYY-MM-DD.
@param [published_before] Only episodes published before this date, YYYY-MM-DD.
@param [only] list_episodes: archived or unarchived.
@param [episodes] Only these episode uuids, comma-separated.
@param [all] archive, unarchive: true to select every episode when no filter is given.
@param [apply] unsubscribe, delete_folder, archive, unarchive: true to do it. Without it the call is a dry run.
@param [max_rows] list_episodes: rows to print (default 200).
@call
END
curry --base:@@=github:Metta-AI/caos?rev=74d72c8f5a66a9fb81b580033b8aa24242712a76&dir=std/go --worker1:@=worker.go --help=$HELP
